    "description": "New Payout Model picklist controlling which commercial fields apply, with a Rev Share % field that only appears for hybrid.\n\n=== FIELDS ===\n\n* Payout Model — Picklist: CPA; Rev Share; Hybrid (CPA + Rev Share). Exact labels not locked.\n\n* Rev Share % — Percent — visible only when Payout Model = Hybrid (or Rev Share)\n\n* CPA Amount — existing field, retained\n\n=== IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS ===\n\n* Genuinely new, confirmed distinct from the old CPA Target Type after Kobi checked its values live ('I think this is a new field').\n\n* Joyce's driver: 'sometimes these operators would pay us based off of CPAs, but then there's also the option to have a rev share or a hybrid where it's CPA plus rev share.'\n\n* Conditional visibility via Dynamic Forms. Helper text on Payout Model: 'Controls which commercial fields apply below.'\n\n=== OPEN QUESTIONS ===\n\n* Kobi never explicitly confirmed the conditional field. Joyce asked 'could another field show up for RevShare and then it not show up if I pick only CPA?'; Waleed said 'Yes, if it's a hybrid'; Kobi's reply on the transcript is just 'Okay. CPA amount.' Treated as in scope — confirm.\n\n* Should Rev Share % also show when Payout Model = Rev Share only, or Hybrid only? Joyce only described the hybrid case.\n\n=== NOTES ===\n\n* The original card body already had the three values and the conditional field. Added API-name placeholders, the distinctness note vs CPA Target Type, and flagged the unconfirmed conditional behaviour.\n\n=== SOURCE ===\n\n* Aug 11 call — Joyce 48:00-49:16\n\nDependencies: None\n\nRemember to update the requirements documentation as part of this change.\n\nPolished 2026-08-17 from the Operator/Partner ticket review, approved by Kobi.",
